{"id":"22.01.PongCylinder","contentHtml":"<p>This project is my solo development of a hyper-casual game reimagining the classic <code>Pong</code> in a three-dimensional cylindrical space.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Goal:</strong> create a unique gaming experience based on custom physics and achieve stylish visuals without expensive performance post-effects.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<hr>\n<h2>Challenge</h2>\n<p>The project set two key tasks:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Gameplay:</strong> Make the ball move not in a straight line, but along a complex parabolic trajectory <strong>curving around the cylinder</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>Technical:</strong> Achieve a bright <code>bloom effect</code> <strong>without using standard Post-Processing</strong> to preserve performance on mobile devices.</li>\n</ol>\n<hr>\n<h2>Engineering Solution</h2>\n<p>To solve these tasks, I developed two key components: a trajectory calculation system and a custom shader for \"fake\" bloom.</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Custom Flight Physics:</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>Instead of using the standard Unity physics engine, the ball's trajectory is <strong>fully calculated via code</strong>.</li>\n<li>The algorithm simulates flight along a parabola in a <mark>cylindrical coordinate system</mark>, which forces the ball to elegantly curve around the central axis.</li>\n<li>The bounce angle depends on the <strong>player's reaction</strong>: precise pressing at the moment of impact directs the ball up in a spiral, and a mistake dampens progress.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Optimized \"Fake Bloom\" on Shaders:</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>Instead of an expensive post-effect, I created a <strong>lightweight alternative</strong>. Simple textured quads are attached to each platform.</li>\n<li>Using an <code>HLSL</code> shader, these quads are <strong>always rotated towards the camera</strong> (\"billboarding\" technique), creating an illusion of glow indistinguishable from real <code>bloom</code>. This solution has practically no effect on performance.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<hr>\n<h2>Outcome</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Unique Gameplay:</strong> Successfully implemented core mechanics with non-standard, memorable flight physics.</li>\n<li><strong>High Performance:</strong> \"Fake Bloom\" on shaders allowed achieving the desired visuals <strong>without FPS drop</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>Complex Skills:</strong> The project demonstrates competencies in both <strong>gameplay programming</strong> (custom physics) and <strong>technical art</strong> (optimized shaders).</li>\n</ul>\n","published":true,"title":"PongCylinder","date":"2022-01","type":"project","tagsArray":["Mobile","Hypercasual","Unity","C#","Blender","HLSL"],"heroVideo":["oPoH8_gt43A"],"shortDescription":"<p>Solo project featuring <strong>custom flight physics</strong> and an optimized <mark>“fake” bloom effect</mark> based on shaders.</p>\n","role":"solo","projectIcon":"/images/projects/22.01.PongCylinder/icon.webp","cardBackground":"/images/projects/22.01.PongCylinder/card.video?v=1765111400775&webm=1&mp4=1","screenshots":[{"src":"/images/projects/22.01.PongCylinder/screenshots/1.webp","width":1080,"height":1920},{"src":"/images/projects/22.01.PongCylinder/screenshots/2.webp","width":1080,"height":1920},{"src":"/images/projects/22.01.PongCylinder/screenshots/3.webp","width":1080,"height":1920}]}